<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Research services"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/research-services/"}>{"Research services"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-42"}>{"Evidence synthesis "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-43"}>{"Design & protocol "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-44"}>{"Data & statistics "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Scope the study "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-42"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l sbdrop__l--2"} style={{ '--rows': "4" }}> <a href={"/services/research-services/systematic-review/"}>{"Systematic review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/scoping-review/"}>{"Scoping review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/rapid-review/"}>{"Rapid & targeted review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/living-systematic-review/"}>{"Living systematic review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/evidence-gap-map/"}>{"Evidence gap map"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/meta-analysis/"}>{"Meta-analysis"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/network-meta-analysis/"}>{"Network meta-analysis & ITC"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/umbrella-review/"}>{"Umbrella review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"}>{"Literature review & gap"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-43"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"}>{"Experimental design"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/statistical-analysis-plan/"}>{"Statistical analysis plan"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/grant-writing/"}>{"Grant writing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-44"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"}>{"Biostatistics & programming"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/redcap-database-build/"}>{"REDCap database build"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/data-management-plan/"}>{"Data management plan"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/cdisc-sdtm-adam/"}>{"CDISC SDTM & ADaM"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/research-services/"}>{"Research services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Grant Writing Service"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Grant Writing Services"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Grant writing by Pubrica’s subject matter experts, built to the rubric your funder actually scores against. "}<b>{"Funding is lost on the criteria far more often than on the science"}</b>{", and every major funder publishes exactly what its reviewers are asked."}</p> <ul className={"hpts"}> <li><b>{"Funding opportunity sourcing and a fit assessment"}</b>{" before you spend months on the wrong call"}</li> <li><b>{"Proposal writing to the funder’s own review criteria"}</b>{" — NIH, Horizon Europe, Wellcome, NSF or national schemes"}</li> <li><b>{"Pre-submission peer review"}</b>{" by readers scoring it the way the panel will"}</li> <li><b>{"Budget and justification"}</b>{" built to the scheme’s eligible-cost rules"}</li> <li><b>{"Resubmission and rebuttal support"}</b>{", answering the panel point by point"}</li> </ul> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Send your draft or your call"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-gw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-gw"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"Proposal at a glance"}</b>{" · one funded application"}</span> <span>{"Horizon Europe RIA · 12 partners"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Funder and scheme settled before a word was drafted"}</b><span>{"RIA, not IA"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Every criterion clear of its own threshold of 3"}</b><span>{"4.5 · 4.0 · 4.5"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Impact written as a pathway, not as a promise"}</b><span>{"Above threshold"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Effort and budget justified partner by partner"}</b><span>{"12 of 12"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Submitted before the portal’s closing afternoon"}</b><span>{"6 days early"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Call"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" fit "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" outline "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" draft "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" mock panel "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"submission"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-what-we-do-l4mhdv"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-who-we-serve-2zqwgx"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-our-compliance-1gfep7i"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-how-it-works-1evc1pb"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-our-experts-15wsn6u"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-sample-work-ufqyeq"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-packages-q097pr"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-guarantee-1qzlo4m"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-client-stories-bjy52r"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-grant-writing-faq-1i78pro"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-what-we-do-l4mhdv"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we do"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six pieces of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Our grant proposal writing services are offered in parts, because applications arrive at every stage — some as a sentence, some as a draft a panel has already turned down once."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Funding opportunity sourcing and fit"}</b> <span>{"Which calls your work is actually eligible for and competitive in, across government funding bodies, charitable foundations, industry programmes and institutional schemes — with the fit argued rather than asserted. We also look at what each funder has recently paid for in your area, because a portfolio that already contains three projects like yours is a different proposition from one that contains none."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Research grant proposal writing"}</b> <span>{"End-to-end drafting from concept to submission: the case for support, aims, background, methodology, feasibility, impact, workplan and the annexes. Written against the criteria that will be applied, in the order the reviewer reads them, and shaped in conversation with you and your co-investigators rather than assembled from what you sent."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Pre-submission peer review of your proposal"}</b> <span>{"A mock panel for a proposal you have already drafted. Two reviewers who have not seen it score it against the funder’s own criteria, write the critique a real panel would write, and rank the changes by how much each would move the score. This grant review is the service that most often changes an outcome, and it is the cheapest thing on this page."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Grant proposal editing and compliance check"}</b> <span>{"Grant editing here means language, structure and argument tightened so the case survives a reader who is on their eleventh application of the weekend — then checked line by line against the call: page limits, fonts and margins, mandatory sections, CV formats, annexes and portal fields. Grant proposal editing that stops at the prose has left the most avoidable failure untouched."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Budgeting and justification"}</b> <span>{"A budget built up from the workplan, costed to the funder’s categories, and justified in the language the rules use. Staff effort by work package, equipment against the cost principles that govern it, indirect costs treated correctly for the scheme, and every line answering the question a reviewer actually asks, which is whether the money buys the work rather than whether the total is modest."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Resubmission and rebuttal support"}</b> <span>{"For a proposal that has been rejected: what the panel actually said as against what it appeared to say, which criticisms are answerable and which point at a real weakness, and whether this scheme is worth a second attempt at all. Then the introduction or response document the funder allows, written so the changes are visible to a reviewer who may not be the one who wrote the comments."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Funders and schemes"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Fifteen kinds of application, and what each one rewards."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Across national agencies, European programmes, charitable foundations, industry schemes and institutional funds — each written to its own rubric rather than to a house template."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"NIH research project grants"}</b><span>{"R01, R21, R03 and the cooperative agreements, under the simplified review framework in force for due dates from 25 January 2025 — where importance and rigour are scored separately and expertise and resources are rated rather than scored."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"NIH resubmissions"}</b><span>{"The single permitted resubmission, with the introduction that has to answer the previous critique in one page and still read as a proposal rather than as a grievance."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"NIH career development and fellowships"}</b><span>{"K and F series, where the candidate, the training plan and the mentor’s record are assessed alongside the science, and a strong project with a thin training plan routinely loses."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"NSF proposals"}</b><span>{"Intellectual merit and broader impacts written as two genuine criteria rather than one criterion and an appendix, with the project description built to the solicitation rather than to the general guide."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"SBIR and STTR"}</b><span>{"Commercialisation-led applications where the technical narrative has to carry a business case, and the reviewer is asking who buys this and at what price as well as whether it works."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Horizon Europe collaborative actions"}</b><span>{"Research and Innovation Actions and Innovation Actions: three criteria, each with a threshold, and an impact pathway that has to connect to the outcomes the work programme itself named."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Horizon Europe two-stage calls"}</b><span>{"A short first-stage application assessed on excellence and impact alone, against a higher per-criterion threshold — a genuinely different document from the full proposal, and rarely a shortened version of it."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Marie Skłodowska-Curie actions"}</b><span>{"Postdoctoral fellowships and doctoral networks, where the training, the supervision and the two-way transfer of knowledge are scored, and the host’s role is assessed as closely as the researcher’s."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"ERC frontier grants"}</b><span>{"Starting, Consolidator, Advanced and the new ERC Plus scheme, where excellence is the sole criterion, the first step reads only the extended synopsis and the CV, and interviews now sit at the second step."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"UKRI and Wellcome"}</b><span>{"Research council standard grants and Wellcome’s Discovery Awards, where half the assessment turns on whether the proposal is bold and a quarter on a research environment written with your institution rather than by you."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Global health and development funders"}</b><span>{"The Gates Foundation, WHO, UNDP and bilateral development programmes, where the question is what changes for a population and by when, and the theory of change is a document rather than a paragraph."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Indian national funders"}</b><span>{"ICMR, DBT, DST, SERB, BIRAC and CSIR, submitted through their own portals and written to their own word caps — a summary in 250 words and a problem statement in 500 is a constraint that decides the application."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"CSR and foundation funding in India"}</b><span>{"Corporate social responsibility proposals under Section 135 of the Companies Act, and applications to charitable trusts and disease foundations, where community benefit and governance are assessed alongside the science."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Industry R&D and partnership funding"}</b><span>{"Public-private partnerships, matched and translational funding, and collaborative awards where an industrial partner’s commitment has to be evidenced rather than described."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Institutional and seed funding"}</b><span>{"Internal competitions, pump-priming awards and small charitable grants — short applications with a low ceiling, which are the sensible way to generate the preliminary data a larger scheme will demand."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"And the fields they are written for"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Proposals are written by people who know the field they are for, across oncology, cardiology, neurology and psychiatry, infectious disease and vaccines, immunology, endocrinology, respiratory and critical care, surgery, rare disease, medical devices and diagnostics, digital health and clinical artificial intelligence, nutrition, public health and epidemiology, health policy and services research, environmental and occupational health, veterinary science, engineering and materials, and preclinical and translational biology. Where a proposal sits between fields — a device with a behavioural endpoint, a machine learning method with a clinical claim — so does the team, because those are the applications that read as impressive to one reviewer and as unconvincing to the one sitting next to them."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-who-we-serve-2zqwgx"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions a proposal."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of applicant commission our research grant writing services, and they arrive with the same underlying request: make this document score well with the people who will actually read it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Academic researchers and universities"}</b><span>{"Faculty, postdoctoral researchers and research offices applying for national and international funding — research proposal writing services for first grants, programme renewals and the fellowship applications that decide a career stage."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Clinicians and hospital research teams"}</b><span>{"Clinical research grant writing for trials, health services research and public health programmes, written by people who know what an ethics committee and a funding panel each need to see and how those two documents differ."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Nonprofits, NGOs and charitable trusts"}</b><span>{"Advocacy, development and community organisations applying to government programmes and private foundations, where the assessment turns on need, governance and what changes for people rather than on novelty alone."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Biotech, pharmaceutical and industry partners"}</b><span>{"Start-ups and established companies applying for research and development funding, SBIR and STTR programmes, translational schemes and public-private partnerships, where a technical narrative has to carry a commercial argument."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Independent researchers and consultants"}</b><span>{"Applicants without a grants office behind them, who need the eligibility check, the compliance check and the institutional formalities handled as carefully as the science."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Government and public sector bodies"}</b><span>{"Local, regional and national bodies commissioning proposals that have to satisfy a funder’s criteria and a policy objective at once, and be defensible to both afterwards."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"The three moments people call"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The best one is when the call opens, or before it does, when the idea can still be shaped around what this funder buys and the team can still be built rather than assembled. The second is three or four weeks out, with a real draft in hand — late enough to be reviewing something honest, early enough that the rewrite list can be acted on, and the point at which a mock panel is worth most. The third is after a rejection, which is a better moment than it feels: the summary statement is the only direct evidence you will ever get about how that panel reads, and it is worth an hour with someone who reads them regularly before you decide whether to resubmit, redirect or stop. What we cannot do is write a serious application in the five days before a deadline. We will say so rather than take the work and deliver something that wastes your submission."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-our-compliance-1gfep7i"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The rules a proposal is held to."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Pubrica works in compliance with this funding agency guidance. Compliance is not a final check here — a proposal that breaks one of a funding body’s formatting or eligibility rules is frequently rejected without being read, and no amount of scientific strength survives that."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Funding agency guidance"}>{"AGENCY"}<em>{"the call itself"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"The funder’s own guidance "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(the document nobody reads twice)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The NIH application guide and its page limits, the Horizon Europe General Annexes and the Part B template attached to your specific topic, the ERC Work Programme, Wellcome’s scheme page, ICMR’s extramural guidelines and the e-PMS forms. These change every cycle, and they change in ways that matter: a page limit reduced, an interview moved to a later step, a criterion reworded. We read the current version for your call rather than the version that was current when somebody last wrote this kind of proposal."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Uniform Guidance 2 CFR 200"}>{"2 CFR 200"}<em>{"Uniform Guidance"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Budgetary and financial accuracy "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(Uniform Guidance, 2 CFR Part 200)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The cost principles that govern United States federal awards: what is allowable, what is allocable, how indirect costs are treated and what has to be justified rather than simply listed. Equivalent rules apply elsewhere — Horizon Europe’s unit and actual-cost categories, UKRI’s full economic costing, ICMR’s recurring and non-recurring heads. A budget that breaks these is not a scoring problem; it is a compliance problem, and it is caught after the science has already been read."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ICMJE and COPE integrity guidance"}>{"ICMJE"}<em>{"COPE"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Research integrity in the proposal "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(ICMJE, COPE)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Proposals make claims about prior work, preliminary data and the applicant’s own contribution, and those claims are checked. Duplicate submission of the same project to two funders without disclosure, preliminary data presented as more settled than it is, and reuse of text from a colleague’s unsuccessful application are all integrity findings rather than drafting slips. We write to the same standard a manuscript is held to, and say where a claim needs softening."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Data management and open science requirements"}>{"DMP"}<em>{"FAIR · open access"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Data management and open science "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(NIH DMS, Horizon Europe, FAIR)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"NIH requires a data management and sharing plan with the application, and reviews it. Horizon Europe expects open science practices inside the methodology it scores, not as an annexe, and mandates open access to publications. These are now scored or screened rather than filed, and a plan written in three sentences the night before reads exactly like one."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Ethics, registration and CSR compliance"}>{"ETHICS"}<em>{"registration · CSR"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Ethics, registration and regional obligations "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(including Section 135, Companies Act)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The ethics self-assessment Horizon Europe requires, the human subjects and vertebrate animal sections NIH scores separately, prospective trial registration where the proposal commits to a trial, and for Indian corporate social responsibility funding the requirements that flow from Section 135 of the Companies Act. Commitments made in a proposal become conditions of the award, so we write only the ones you can keep."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Eligibility, before anything else"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The cheapest mistake to avoid and the most common one we find in drafts that arrive late. Career-stage windows measured from the date of the doctorate rather than from the first appointment, and the specific grounds on which an ERC window may be extended; host institution rules; the minimum consortium composition a Horizon Europe topic sets, which is a condition rather than a preference; resubmission limits, including the restriction a C grade at the ERC carries and the single resubmission NIH allows; and whether an investigator already holds an award that excludes this one. Every one of these is checkable in an afternoon, and every one of them ends an application that has taken four months. We check them in the first conversation, before any writing is quoted — and you can run the mechanical part yourself first with the "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/free-tools/#grant-eligibility"} data-nav={""}>{"free grant eligibility checker"}</a>{", which carries the published rule for eight schemes beside its answer."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"A reviewer can tell. That is the whole risk."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Funders have begun saying plainly that applications reading as machine-generated will be treated as a weakness, and several now require a declaration. A proposal is judged on conviction as much as content, and conviction is the first thing that goes."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Checking the draft against the call’s own rubric, criterion by criterion. Finding prior work and policy context. Consistency between the case for support, the workplan and the budget justification."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Writing the case for support; the track-record or team sections; anything describing what you will do and why you are the person to do it; and any submission where the funder asks for a declaration and it has not been made."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-how-it-works-1evc1pb"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How our grant writing service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Our step-by-step process."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Twelve stages across six phases, each owned by the Pubrica specialist qualified to own it — a subject specialist, a grant writing expert, a statistician, a costing specialist and an outside reader who has not seen the proposal before."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stages one and two"}</span> <h3>{"Fit, eligibility and the rubric"}</h3> <p><b>{"Grant writing consultants."}</b>{" Which call, which scheme, and whether you are eligible for it — settled before any drafting. Then the rubric itself: the criteria that will be used, their scales and thresholds, the weightings, the page limits, and what this particular funder does not assess at all. Everything after this stage is written against that document."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stages three and four"}</span> <h3>{"Novelty, gap and the case for support"}</h3> <p><b>{"Subject specialists."}</b>{" A search of the funded landscape as well as the literature — what this funder has already paid for in this area, which is a different question from what has been published. Then the gap stated so a reviewer can verify it, and the aims written to be distinct, non-contingent and answerable rather than sequential."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stages five and six"}</span> <h3>{"Methodology, feasibility and the statistics"}</h3> <p><b>{"Methodologists and statisticians."}</b>{" The design, the power calculation and the analysis plan written to the level the funder scores rather than the level a paper reports. Pitfalls named and an alternative given for each, because a proposal that anticipates its own failure modes reads as feasible and one that does not reads as optimistic."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stages seven and eight"}</span> <h3>{"Impact, dissemination and the workplan"}</h3> <p><b>{"Grant writing experts."}</b>{" Where the funder scores impact, the beneficiaries are named, the route to each is described and the measure is stated — with dissemination, exploitation and communication written as the three separate things the evaluators are asked about. Then work packages, deliverables, milestones, dependencies and a risk register that names risks a reviewer would have raised anyway."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stages nine and ten"}</span> <h3>{"Budget, justification and the annexes"}</h3> <p><b>{"Costing specialists and project coordinators."}</b>{" A budget and budget justification built from the workplan rather than fitted to the ceiling, with every line justified in the terms the funder uses and effort allocated per partner. Alongside it the annexes that quietly fail applications: letters of support that say something, the data management plan, the ethics self-assessment, CVs in the funder’s format, and the Gantt chart and logic model where they are expected."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stages eleven and twelve"}</span> <h3>{"Mock panel, compliance check and submission"}</h3> <p><b>{"An outside reader, then a compliance check."}</b>{" Two reviewers who have not seen the proposal score it against the funder’s own criteria and write the critique a panel would write. Their comments are addressed, then everything is checked against the call: page limits, fonts and margins, mandatory sections, annexes, portal fields. We aim to submit days early, because portals fail on the closing afternoon and funders do not extend for it."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} style={{ borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)", background: "var(--paper-2)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the call and the idea. We will tell you whether it is worth writing."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Before anything is quoted, a grant writing consultant reads your idea against the call you are aiming at and tells you whether you are eligible, whether the fit is real, and which criterion is going to be hardest for you specifically. Two business days, at no cost. Sometimes the answer is that a different scheme fits better, or that this call is not worth four months — which is the cheapest thing anyone will tell you all year."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The call"}</b><span>{"The funder, the scheme and the deadline"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The idea"}</b><span>{"An outline, an abstract or a paragraph"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"What exists"}</b><span>{"Preliminary data, prior publications"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The team"}</b><span>{"Investigators, partners, CVs"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Any draft"}</b><span>{"A part-written proposal, if you have one"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Any feedback"}</b><span>{"Reviewer comments from a previous attempt"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"If you have been rejected before, the reviewer comments are the most valuable thing you can send and the thing applicants most often leave out, usually because reading them again is unpleasant. They are the only direct evidence of how that panel reads, and a resubmission that does not visibly answer them tends to attract the same criticism a second time."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"fmb"}> <div className={"wrap fmb__in"}> <p className={"fmb__lab"}>{"Why strong proposals lose"}</p> <h2 className={"fmb__h"}>{"Most rejected proposals from good groups are not weak. They are misaddressed."}</h2> <ol className={"fmb__list"}> <li><b>{"Written for the wrong reader"}</b><span>{"A Horizon Europe impact case, where impact is a third of the score and a hard gate, arriving at the "}<i>{"ERC — where impact earns nothing at all"}</i>{". Five pages, at the step that removes most applicants."}</span></li> <li><b>{"Polished on the criterion that cannot lift it"}</b><span>{"NIH now instructs reviewers that the importance of the research "}<i>{"sets the ceiling"}</i>{" on the best possible overall impact score. No amount of work on the approach raises it past that."}</span></li> <li><b>{"Eligible on paper, not in the call"}</b><span>{"A career window that moved, a consortium missing an EU Member State, a resubmission already used. "}<i>{"Checkable in an afternoon"}</i>{" — and each one ends four months of writing."}</span></li> <li><b>{"Answering a question the form did not ask"}</b><span>{"ICMR asks whether the study is likely to affect health outcomes, in five hundred words. A European impact pathway "}<i>{"does not fit in that box"}</i>{" and does not score in it."}</span></li> </ol> <p className={"fmb__foot"}><b>{"The research was rarely the problem."}</b>{" We write and review against the rubric that will actually be used, criterion by criterion, in the order the panel has been instructed to read it — and we check eligibility before any writing is quoted, because that is the failure that costs the most and prevents the least."}</p> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every proposal"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Written to the funder’s own rubric"}</li> <li>{"Read by a mock panel"}</li> <li>{"Budget justified line by line"}</li> <li>{"Compliance checked"}</li> <li>{"Submitted with days in hand"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"1,200+"}</b><span>{"Grant proposals written, reviewed and edited"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Supporting researchers through funding and publication"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"NIH · ERC"}</b><span>{"Horizon Europe, Wellcome, UKRI, ICMR, DBT"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The rubric decides"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"One proposal, scored by five funders. They do not agree."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Describe a proposal once, then move between funders. The same six things about your research produce five different outcomes, because each funder has published a different instruction to its reviewers — and the section you cut for space is the one that decides it somewhere else."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"pnl rv rv-d1"} data-pnl={""}> <div className={"pnl__bar"}> <span><b>{"Set the proposal on the left."}</b>{" Switch funder along the top."}</span> <span data-pnl-frame={""}>{"NIH · R01 · United States"}</span> </div> <div className={"pnl__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Funder"} data-pnl-tabs={""}><button type={"button"} className={"pnl__tab"} role={"tab"} data-f={"nih"} aria-selected={"true"}><b>{"NIH"}</b><span>{"R01 · United States"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"pnl__tab"} role={"tab"} data-f={"heu"} aria-selected={"false"}><b>{"Horizon Europe"}</b><span>{"RIA · European Union"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"pnl__tab"} role={"tab"} data-f={"erc"} aria-selected={"false"}><b>{"ERC"}</b><span>{"Frontier grants · Europe"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"pnl__tab"} role={"tab"} data-f={"wel"} aria-selected={"false"}><b>{"Wellcome"}</b><span>{"Discovery Award · UK"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"pnl__tab"} role={"tab"} data-f={"icmr"} aria-selected={"false"}><b>{"ICMR"}</b><span>{"Extramural ad-hoc · India"}</span></button></div> <div className={"pnl__in"}> <div className={"pnl__ctl"} data-pnl-q={""}><p className={"pnl__ctlk"}>{"Describe the proposal"}</p><div className={"pnl__q"}><p className={"pnl__k"}>{"The question and the gap"}</p><div className={"pnl__seg"} role={"group"} aria-label={"The question and the gap"}><button type={"button"} data-a={"gap"} data-l={"2"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Shown"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"gap"} data-l={"1"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Argued"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"gap"} data-l={"0"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Assumed"}</button></div><p className={"pnl__d"}>{"The gap is asserted in the introduction and supported by a handful of citations."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__q"}><p className={"pnl__k"}>{"Ambition and novelty"}</p><div className={"pnl__seg"} role={"group"} aria-label={"Ambition and novelty"}><button type={"button"} data-a={"nov"} data-l={"2"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Beyond"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"nov"} data-l={"1"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Clearly new"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"nov"} data-l={"0"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Extension"}</button></div><p className={"pnl__d"}>{"Genuinely new work, incremental in scale rather than in kind."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__q"}><p className={"pnl__k"}>{"Approach: methods, rigour, feasibility"}</p><div className={"pnl__seg"} role={"group"} aria-label={"Approach: methods, rigour, feasibility"}><button type={"button"} data-a={"app"} data-l={"2"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Complete"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"app"} data-l={"1"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Described"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"app"} data-l={"0"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Sketched"}</button></div><p className={"pnl__d"}>{"Methods are described; pitfalls and alternatives are thin or absent."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__q"}><p className={"pnl__k"}>{"The investigator and the team"}</p><div className={"pnl__seg"} role={"group"} aria-label={"The investigator and the team"}><button type={"button"} data-a={"pi"} data-l={"2"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"In field"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"pi"} data-l={"1"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Adjacent"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"pi"} data-l={"0"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Emerging"}</button></div><p className={"pnl__d"}>{"A strong record in a neighbouring area, with one method held by a collaborator."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__q"}><p className={"pnl__k"}>{"The impact pathway"}</p><div className={"pnl__seg"} role={"group"} aria-label={"The impact pathway"}><button type={"button"} data-a={"imp"} data-l={"2"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Mapped"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"imp"} data-l={"1"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Stated"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"imp"} data-l={"0"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Implicit"}</button></div><p className={"pnl__d"}>{"A general statement of who will benefit and roughly how."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__q"}><p className={"pnl__k"}>{"Workplan, budget and risk"}</p><div className={"pnl__seg"} role={"group"} aria-label={"Workplan, budget and risk"}><button type={"button"} data-a={"wp"} data-l={"2"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Engineered"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"wp"} data-l={"1"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Present"}</button><button type={"button"} data-a={"wp"} data-l={"0"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Outline"}</button></div><p className={"pnl__d"}>{"A timeline and an itemised budget, without risks or per-partner effort."}</p></div></div> <div className={"pnl__out"} data-pnl-out={""}><p className={"pnl__ok"}>{"What the study section does with it"}</p><h3 className={"pnl__nm"}>{"NIH R01, simplified review framework"}</h3><p className={"pnl__meta"}>{"For due dates on or after 25 January 2025 · Specific Aims 1 page, Research Strategy 12 pages · three factors, two of them scored"}</p><div className={"pnl__crits"}><div className={"pnl__c"}><div className={"pnl__ct"}><p className={"pnl__cn"}>{"Factor 1 — Importance of the Research"}<em>{"Significance, Innovation"}</em></p><span className={"pnl__cv"}><b>{"5"}</b>{" · Good"}</span></div><div><div className={"pnl__n9"}><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"hit"} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /></div><div className={"pnl__n9lab"}><span>{"1 exceptional"}</span><span>{"9 poor"}</span></div></div></div><div className={"pnl__c"}><div className={"pnl__ct"}><p className={"pnl__cn"}>{"Factor 2 — Rigor and Feasibility"}<em>{"Approach"}</em></p><span className={"pnl__cv"}><b>{"5"}</b>{" · Good"}</span></div><div><div className={"pnl__n9"}><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"hit"} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /></div><div className={"pnl__n9lab"}><span>{"1 exceptional"}</span><span>{"9 poor"}</span></div></div></div><div className={"pnl__c"}><div className={"pnl__ct"}><p className={"pnl__cn"}>{"Factor 3 — Expertise and Resources"}<em>{"Investigator, Environment"}</em></p><span className={"pnl__cv"}>{"Appropriate"}</span></div><p className={"pnl__cd"}>{"Not scored. Reviewers rate this factor as appropriate or not, and only the second option carries written comments."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__c"}><div className={"pnl__ct"}><p className={"pnl__cn"}>{"Overall Impact"}<em>{"Assigned holistically, not averaged"}</em></p><span className={"pnl__cv"}><b>{"5"}</b>{" · Good · 50"}</span></div><div><div className={"pnl__n9"}><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"on"} /><i className={"hit"} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /><i className={""} /></div><div className={"pnl__n9lab"}><span>{"1 exceptional"}</span><span>{"9 poor"}</span></div></div><p className={"pnl__cd"}>{"The panel mean of the individual overall impact scores, multiplied by ten, is what appears on the summary statement: 10 at best, 90 at worst."}</p></div></div><div className={"pnl__v pnl__v--bad"}><p><b>{"Discussed at best, and increasingly not even that."}</b>{" Through the October 2026 council round, NIH has cut the share of applications discussed at review to between 30 and 35 per cent, from around half, and sorts the rest into “competitive but not discussed” and “not competitive”. A score that was borderline two years ago is now frequently a score that is never spoken about in the room."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__blind"}><h4>{"What NIH never scores here"}</h4><p><b>{"Your impact pathway."}</b>{" There is no dissemination and exploitation criterion. NIH asks about influence on the field, inside Factor 1 — so the beneficiary mapping that wins a Horizon Europe grant earns nothing on an R01 and costs you page space you do not have."}</p><p><b>{"Your workplan and budget detail"}</b>{" are reviewed for whether the budget is appropriate, but they carry no criterion score of their own."}</p></div><div className={"pnl__move"}><b>{"The single change that moves this the furthest:"}</b>{" the question and the gap, from “Argued” to “Shown”."}</div><p className={"pnl__src"}>{"Factors, the non-scoring of Factor 3, the 1–9 whole-number scale and the instruction that Factor 1 limits the overall impact score are NIH’s own, from the simplified review framework and its reviewer guidance. The reduction in the share of applications discussed is NOT-OD-26-069. NIH has separately asked for comment, to 13 October 2026, on replacing the released numerical score with bands — proposed, not adopted."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"pnl__foot"}><b>{"The criteria, scales, thresholds and ranking rules here are the funders’ own, taken from their current published guidance and cited under each panel."}</b>{" What is ours is the mapping from a description of a proposal onto those rules, which is a simplification: a real reviewer reads the document, not six settings, and is influenced by how well it is written, whether the preliminary data convinces, and what that panel has already read that morning. Funder guidance also changes every cycle — check the call before writing to any figure on this page, including the page limits."}</p> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why a strong proposal still loses"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Most unsuccessful applications from good research groups are not weak. They are misaddressed. A consortium proposal written for Horizon Europe, where impact is a third of the assessment and a hard gate, arrives at the ERC where excellence is the sole criterion and an impact section earns nothing at all — in a five-page document, at the step that eliminates most applicants. An NIH application polished endlessly on its Approach runs into a framework that now instructs reviewers that the importance of the research sets the limit on the best possible overall impact score, so the approach cannot lift it past that ceiling. And a proposal built on a European impact pathway reaches ICMR, which asks whether the study is likely to affect health outcomes, in five hundred words. The research was never the problem. The document was pointed at the wrong reader."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-our-experts-15wsn6u"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-sample-work-ufqyeq"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What a review report contains."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"The mock panel is the service that most often changes an outcome, so it is the one we show. A draft R01 read by two reviewers who had not seen it, scored under NIH’s current framework, with the rewrite list ranked by what each change is worth. Use the tabs to see each part."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Grant proposal review report"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"NIH R01 resubmission · two independent readers · simplified review framework"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"Factor-by-factor critique · predicted overall impact · the rewrite list, ranked"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the grant proposal review report"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"gw-t1"} aria-controls={"gw-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"How it was read"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"gw-t2"} aria-controls={"gw-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"The scores"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"gw-t3"} aria-controls={"gw-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"The critique"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"gw-t4"} aria-controls={"gw-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Rewrite list"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"gw-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"gw-t1"}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"1"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Two readers, scoring independently"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"One from the applicant’s field and one from an adjacent one, because a real study section contains both and they disagree in predictable ways. Neither saw the other’s comments before submitting a score."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"2"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Scored under the framework that will actually be used"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Three factors, two of them scored on 1 to 9 in whole numbers, and expertise and resources rated rather than scored. The critique is written in the form a summary statement takes, not as track changes."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"3"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The previous summary statement read first"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"This is a resubmission, so the earlier critique was read before the new draft. Two of the three earlier criticisms are answered in the current text; the third is answered in the introduction but not in the Research Strategy, where the reviewer will look."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"4"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Read against the clock a reviewer has"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Roughly ninety minutes for a twelve-page Research Strategy, in a batch of eight. Both readers noted where they lost the thread, and those points are reported even where the argument turned out to be sound."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"5"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"What was not assessed"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"We do not predict funding. A score is a prediction about one panel on one day, and institute priorities now sit alongside it in the decision."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Two readers · independent scores · reconciled afterwards"}</span><span>{"Scored as the panel will"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"gw-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"gw-t2"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Factor 1 — Importance"}</dt><dd><b>{"3"}</b>{" · Excellent. Significance and innovation, scored together"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Factor 2 — Rigor and feasibility"}</dt><dd><b>{"5"}</b>{" · Good. The approach, and the weakest part of the application"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Factor 3 — Expertise and resources"}</dt><dd>{"Appropriate, with one comment on a method held by a single collaborator"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Predicted overall impact"}</dt><dd><b>{"4"}</b>{" · Very Good, which is 40 on the summary statement"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reader disagreement"}</dt><dd>{"One factor apart on Factor 2 (5 and 6), agreed on Factor 1"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Ceiling"}</dt><dd>{"Factor 1 limits the best available overall impact score to 3"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"If the approach is fixed"}</dt><dd>{"Overall impact moves to 3; it cannot move past 3 without Factor 1"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Context"}</dt><dd>{"Through the October 2026 council round, 30–35% of applications are discussed"}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"gw-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"gw-t3"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The gap is demonstrated, not asserted"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Both readers accepted the premise without argument, which is rarer than applicants assume and is why Factor 1 sits where it does."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Aim 3 is genuinely independent"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"It does not depend on Aim 1 succeeding. Contingent aims are the most common structural weakness in a resubmission and this draft does not have one."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Aim 2 has no alternative approach"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The assay carrying the primary readout is described once, with no fallback. Both readers raised it independently, and one used the word “fragile”. This is the single largest cost to Factor 2."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Power stated without its assumptions"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The sample size appears as a number. The effect size it assumes, and where that effect size came from, are not given — so a reviewer cannot check it and one of the two did not believe it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"One method, one person"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The imaging analysis rests entirely on a collaborator with no letter in the application. Factor 3 was still rated appropriate, and the comment will be written, and comments on that factor are required to affect the overall score."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Three criticisms both readers raised"}</span><span>{"Two strengths worth protecting in the rewrite"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"gw-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"gw-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"1 · Highest value"}</dt><dd>{"Give Aim 2 a stated alternative approach and a decision point for switching to it"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"2"}</dt><dd>{"Show the power calculation’s assumptions and cite where the effect size came from"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"3"}</dt><dd>{"Obtain a letter from the imaging collaborator that commits time, not enthusiasm"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"4"}</dt><dd>{"Move the answer to the third earlier criticism into the Research Strategy itself"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"5"}</dt><dd>{"Cut the second background page; both readers lost the thread there and it buys nothing"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Worth together"}</dt><dd>{"Factor 2 from 5 to 3, and the overall impact from 4 to 3"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Not on the list"}</dt><dd>{"Further work on significance — Factor 1 is already at 3 and the writing is not what holds it there"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Time required"}</dt><dd>{"Around three days of the PI’s attention, and one letter with two weeks of notice"}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · applicant and project details changed"}</span><span data-docpage={""}>{"Page 1 of 4"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"The report is the critique and the arithmetic behind it. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each part."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The rewrite list is ranked by what each change is worth"}</b>{", not by how much work it is. That ordering is the useful part: applicants reliably spend their remaining fortnight on the section they enjoy rewriting, and it is reliably not the section holding the score down."}</p> <p><b>{"It also says what not to do."}</b>{" Here, more work on significance would have been wasted — Factor 1 is already the ceiling, and the writing is not what put it there. Telling a client to stop working on something is usually the most valuable sentence in the document."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Two readers, scoring blind"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"One in field, one adjacent, reconciled after the fact."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Scored on the funder’s own scale"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Not a house rating invented for the report."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Changes ranked by score movement"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With the arithmetic shown, including its ceiling."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"No prediction of funding"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"A score is not a decision, and we do not pretend otherwise."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a review report built round an application like yours — same funder, same scheme, same field."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-gw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-gw"}>{"Read the full report"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-gw"}> <span><b>{"Read the full review report"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — how it was read, the scores, the critique and the rewrite list"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-gw"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Grant writing · sample review report"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Grant proposal review report"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"NIH R01 resubmission · two independent readers · scored under the simplified review framework · factor-by-factor critique, predicted overall impact, and the rewrite list ranked by what each change is worth. Applicant, institution and project details have been removed or changed. Ask us and we will send one built around an application like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"How this was read"}</h4> <p>{"A mock panel, run the way the real one is run rather than the way an edit is run. Two readers scored the application independently before seeing each other’s comments, and the critique below is written in the form a summary statement takes."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"How it was handled"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Readers"}</td><td>{"Two. One from the applicant’s own field, one from an adjacent field, because a study section contains both and they disagree in predictable ways."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Framework"}</td><td>{"The simplified review framework, in force for due dates from 25 January 2025: Factor 1 and Factor 2 scored 1–9 in whole numbers, Factor 3 rated rather than scored."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Prior critique"}</td><td>{"Read first. This is a resubmission, so the earlier summary statement set the questions the new draft has to answer."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Time"}</td><td>{"Ninety minutes each for a twelve-page Research Strategy, which is roughly what a reviewer carrying eight applications actually gives it."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reconciliation"}</td><td>{"Scores compared after both were fixed. Where the readers differed, both positions are reported rather than averaged into one."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"What this is not: a prediction of funding. A score describes one panel on one day, and since 2025 institute priorities and strategic considerations sit alongside the score in the decision rather than behind a published payline."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"The scores"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Factor"}</th><th>{"Score"}</th><th>{"What it covers, and what the readers concluded"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td><b>{"Factor 1"}</b><br />{"Importance of the Research"}</td><td><b>{"3"}</b><br />{"Excellent"}</td><td>{"Significance and innovation, scored together. Both readers accepted the premise without argument, which is less common than applicants assume. Neither thought the question was merely incremental."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Factor 2"}</b><br />{"Rigor and Feasibility"}</td><td><b>{"5"}</b><br />{"Good"}</td><td>{"The approach. The weakest part of the application, and the only factor on which the readers differed — 5 and 6. Both raised the same underlying problem."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Factor 3"}</b><br />{"Expertise and Resources"}</td><td>{"Appropriate"}</td><td>{"Not scored; reviewers rate it as appropriate or as needing additional expertise or resources. Rated appropriate here, with one written comment on a method that rests on a single collaborator."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Overall impact"}</b></td><td><b>{"4"}</b><br />{"Very Good"}</td><td>{"Assigned holistically. NIH instructs reviewers not to average the two scored factors, and tells them the Factor 1 score sets the limit on the best possible overall impact score."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__cl"}><b>{"The arithmetic that matters for the rewrite."}</b>{" Factor 1 at 3 caps the overall impact at 3. Repairing the approach moves the overall from 4 to 3 and no further; nothing in the Research Strategy can take it past 3 while Factor 1 stays where it is. That single fact decides what is worth doing in the fortnight available — and it means further work on the significance section would buy nothing, because the writing is not what is holding Factor 1 at 3."}</p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Context the score should be read against: through the October 2026 Advisory Council round, NIH has reduced the share of applications discussed at review to between 30 and 35 per cent, from around half, and sorts the remainder into applications that were competitive but not discussed and those that were not. A score that would have been discussed two years ago may now not be."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"The critique"}</h4> <h5>{"What is working, and should survive the rewrite"}</h5> <ul> <li><b>{"The gap is demonstrated rather than asserted."}</b>{" The reader from the adjacent field could check the claim from the cited work without taking it on trust, and did. This is what is holding Factor 1 at 3 rather than at 5, and it is the easiest thing to damage while cutting for space."}</li> <li><b>{"Aim 3 does not depend on Aim 1 succeeding."}</b>{" Contingent aims are the most common structural weakness in a resubmission, because a reviewer who doubts the first aim then doubts all of them. This draft does not have that problem, and the independence should be made more visible, not less."}</li> </ul> <h5>{"What both readers raised independently"}</h5> <ul> <li><b>{"Aim 2 has no alternative approach."}</b>{" The assay carrying the primary readout is described once, with no fallback and no decision point at which the team would switch. One reader used the word “fragile”. This is the single largest cost to Factor 2 and the first thing to fix."}</li> <li><b>{"The power calculation appears as a number."}</b>{" The effect size it assumes, and the source of that effect size, are not given, so a reviewer cannot check it. One of the two readers did not believe it, and said so in a way that would have appeared in a real critique."}</li> <li><b>{"One method rests on one person."}</b>{" The imaging analysis depends entirely on a collaborator with no letter in the application. Factor 3 was still rated appropriate, but the comment will be written, and reviewers are instructed that gaps in expertise or resources should affect the overall score."}</li> </ul> <h5>{"Two further comments, from one reader each"}</h5> <ul> <li><b>{"The third criticism from the previous round is answered in the introduction but not in the Research Strategy."}</b>{" A reviewer looking for the change will look where the science is, and a new reviewer on the panel may not read the introduction closely at all."}</li> <li><b>{"Both readers lost the thread on the second background page."}</b>{" One recovered and one did not. The argument turns out to be sound, which is why this is reported as a writing problem rather than a scientific one — and it is a page that can simply go."}</li> </ul> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"The rewrite list"}</h4> <p>{"Ranked by what each change is worth rather than by how much work it is, because the fortnight before a deadline is reliably spent on the section the applicant most enjoys rewriting."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Change"}</th><th>{"Worth"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"1. Give Aim 2 a stated alternative approach, with the decision point at which the team would switch to it and what would trigger that decision."}</td><td>{"Most of the movement in Factor 2"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"2. Show the power calculation’s assumptions: the effect size, where it came from, and why it is the smallest difference worth detecting."}</td><td>{"Closes the feasibility doubt"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"3. Obtain a letter from the imaging collaborator that commits named time, not enthusiasm."}</td><td>{"Removes the Factor 3 comment"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"4. Move the answer to the third earlier criticism into the Research Strategy itself, leaving a pointer in the introduction."}</td><td>{"Protects against a new reviewer"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"5. Cut the second background page."}</td><td>{"Buys space for items 1 and 2"}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"Together"}</b></td><td><b>{"Factor 2 from 5 to 3, and the"}<br />{"overall impact from 4 to 3"}</b></td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__cl"}><b>{"What is deliberately not on this list."}</b>{" Further work on the significance section. Factor 1 is already at 3, it is the ceiling on the overall score, and the writing is not what is holding it there — so time spent polishing it is time taken from the two changes that do move the score. Telling an applicant to stop working on something is usually the most useful sentence in this document."}</p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Estimated cost of the list: around three days of the principal investigator’s attention, plus one letter that needs a fortnight of notice. Item 3 is the one that has to be started today."}</p> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"What is handed over"}</h4> <ul> <li>{"The two readers’ independent critiques, unedited, with their scores as first recorded."}</li> <li>{"The reconciled report: factor-by-factor findings, with the points both readers raised marked."}</li> <li>{"The predicted overall impact score, with the reasoning and the ceiling stated explicitly."}</li> <li>{"The rewrite list, ranked by score movement, with an estimate of what each change costs in time."}</li> <li>{"A compliance check against the funding opportunity: page limits, formatting, mandatory sections and annexes."}</li> <li>{"A marked-up copy of the proposal, keyed to the numbered items in the rewrite list."}</li> </ul> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Pubrica supports the application; the science, the claims and the accountability remain yours, and the proposal is submitted in your name by your institution. We do not become an undeclared author, and where a funder asks whether professional assistance was used we help you say so. Any AI assistance in drafting is declared."}</p> <div className={"fsm__end"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-grant-writing-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"ba rv"}> <div className={"ba__hd"}><span><b>{"Before and after"}</b>{" · the opening of a Specific Aims page, redacted"}</span><span>{"NIH R01 · resubmission"}</span></div> <div className={"ba__g"}> <div className={"ba__c ba__c--b"}> <p className={"ba__k"}>{"As it arrived"}</p> <p className={"ba__t"}>{"Cardiovascular disease is the leading cause of death worldwide, accounting for 17.9 million deaths each year. Despite advances in treatment, outcomes remain poor in certain populations."}</p> <ul className={"ba__f"}><li><span>{"The most valuable sentence on the most valuable page, spent telling a cardiology panel what cardiology is."}</span></li><li><span>{"No gap, no claim and no question by the end of the paragraph."}</span></li><li><span>{"“Certain populations” where the proposal needs a named one."}</span></li><li><span>{"Under the current NIH framework the importance of the research sets the ceiling on the overall impact score — and this paragraph is where importance is argued."}</span></li></ul> </div> <div className={"ba__c ba__c--a"}> <p className={"ba__k"}>{"As it went out"}</p> <p className={"ba__t"}>{"Guideline-directed therapy reduces mortality by a third in heart failure, yet fewer than one patient in five receiving dialysis is prescribed it — because every trial that established the benefit excluded them. We have shown in a 4,200-patient cohort that the association holds in this group. This proposal tests it directly: we will determine whether initiation improves survival at 24 months, in whom the benefit is largest, and at what cost in hyperkalaemia."}</p> <ul className={"ba__f"}><li><span>{"The gap is specific, evidenced, and the reason for it is named."}</span></li><li><span>{"Preliminary data appears in the first paragraph rather than on page four."}</span></li><li><span>{"The aims are testable statements a reviewer can score, not areas of interest."}</span></li><li><span>{"It argues importance where the framework says importance is decided."}</span></li></ul> </div> </div> <p className={"ba__foot"}><b>{"Every funder publishes what its reviewers are asked, and the documents disagree with one another."}</b>{" The version on the right was written for the NIH framework. For an ERC application it would be rewritten around excellence and the impact material dropped entirely, because at the ERC impact scores nothing at all."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What a Pubrica proposal delivers"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it gives you."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A proposal a panel can score highly without having to work for it, and four months of your own time back."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Written to the rubric that will be used"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Every section earns its space against a published criterion, and the sections this funder does not assess are cut rather than trimmed. That is where page space comes from in a document capped at five, twelve or forty pages — and page space is what a reviewer notices the absence of first."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The weak criterion found before the panel finds it"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Funders eliminate on the lowest criterion far more often than they reward the highest. A mock panel that scores your draft criterion by criterion tells you which one is going to end it, at a point when a fortnight of work can still move it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Your own time spent where it is worth most"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"A serious application takes a principal investigator between six and twelve full working days, spread across months of small interruptions. Most of that is drafting, formatting, chasing CVs and rebuilding budgets. The parts only you can do — the idea, the judgement, the collaborators — are a fraction of it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"A document that does not fail on a technicality"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Eligibility, page limits, fonts, mandatory annexes, CV formats, portal fields and the closing afternoon itself. These end applications that were going to be funded, they are entirely preventable, and they are prevented by a specialist whose job it is rather than by the person who wrote the science."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-packages-q097pr"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Four ways in, depending on how much of it exists already."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Every package is run by a grant writing expert with a subject specialist, a statistician and a costing specialist drawn in as the application needs them, and a dedicated project coordinator who owns the deadline."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"trn rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"trn__i"}><p className={"trn__k"}>{"Rush"}</p><p className={"trn__v"}>{"1 week"}</p><p className={"trn__d"}>{"Where capacity allows. Quoted on capacity rather than on urgency, so a rush is not a surcharge for your deadline."}</p></div> <div className={"trn__i"}><p className={"trn__k"}>{"Standard"}</p><p className={"trn__v"}>{"2–3 weeks"}</p><p className={"trn__d"}>{"The normal route, and the one that leaves room for a revision round before your own deadline."}</p></div> <div className={"trn__i"}><p className={"trn__k"}>{"Extended"}</p><p className={"trn__v"}>{"4–5 weeks"}</p><p className={"trn__d"}>{"Larger scopes, multi-database searches, and anything needing a second reviewer throughout."}</p></div> </div> <div className={"tiers tiers--4 rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Basic"}</span> <h3>{"Proposal review and editing"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Applicants with a complete draft who want it scored and sharpened before it goes"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $390"}</b><span>{"one proposal · one funder’s criteria · two readers"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"5–7 working days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Mock panel: two readers scoring against the funder’s own criteria"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Structural and language editing of the full proposal"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Formatting to the funder’s template and page limits"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Compliance check against the call, including eligibility"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Rewrite list ranked by score movement"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: budget rebuild; annexes; resubmission support."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-gw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-gw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Basic"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Standard"}</span> <h3>{"Proposal writing"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Applicants with objectives, a team and data ready, who need the proposal itself written"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $1,850"}</b><span>{"single investigator · one funder · budget included"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15–20 working days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Basic"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Full drafting: summary, aims, background, methodology and impact"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Budget and justification built from the workplan"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Timeline, milestones and deliverables"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Two rounds of revision with the writer"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: full annexe set; letters; portal submission support."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-gw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-gw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Standard"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Premium"}</span> <h3>{"End-to-end support"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"First-time applicants, large programme grants and multi-partner consortia"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $2,750"}</b><span>{"one call · every annex · submission handled"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"By the call deadline"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Standard"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Funding opportunity sourcing and the fit argument"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Concept development, background and needs assessment"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"All annexes: data management plan, ethics self-assessment, CVs, letters"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Gantt chart, logic model and risk register"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Submission support, and post-submission consultation if the panel comes back"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Consortium coordination across partners sits here."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-gw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-gw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Premium"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Custom"}</span> <h3>{"Resubmission and rescue"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Rejected proposals, and applications with less time left than they need"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $890"}</b><span>{"one summary statement · one resubmission"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"By project scope"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reviewer comments analysed for what they actually say"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"An honest view on whether this scheme is worth a second attempt"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The introduction or response document the funder allows"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Redirection to a better-fitting call where that is the right answer"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Short-deadline work is quoted on capacity, not urgency."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-gw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-gw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Custom"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Success commission, and the funders we have written for"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}><b>{"On co-created applications we take a 3% commission on the award, and only on the award."}</b>{" It aligns us with the outcome rather than with the page count, and it is the only part of our pricing that depends on whether you are funded. It is optional: every package above can be bought on its fee alone, and we will tell you which arrangement is cheaper for your application rather than which is better for us. What we will not do is make the whole engagement contingent, because a supplier who is paid only on success has an incentive to submit rather than to tell you not to."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"} style={{ marginTop: "14px" }}>{"Applications have been written or reviewed for the National Institutes of Health, the National Science Foundation, the Department of Defense, the Department of Energy, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration, the United States Department of Agriculture, the Small Business Innovation Research and Small Business Technology Transfer programmes, Horizon Europe, the European Research Council, the Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions, the European Innovation Council, UK Research and Innovation, the Medical Research Council, the National Institute for Health and Care Research, the Wellcome Trust, Cancer Research UK, the British Heart Foundation, the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation, the World Health Organization, the United Nations Development Programme, the Indian Council of Medical Research, the Department of Biotechnology, the Department of Science and Technology, the Science and Engineering Research Board, the Biotechnology Industry Research Assistance Council and the Council of Scientific and Industrial Research — twenty-seven in all. We name the funders rather than the awards, because the award belongs to the applicant and the outcome was never ours to claim."}</p> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"The mock panel can be bought on its own, and it is the least expensive thing on this page. Two readers who have not seen your proposal score it against the funder’s criteria and write the critique a panel would write, usually inside a week. Commissioned most often three or four weeks before a deadline, which is late enough to be reading a real proposal and early enough to act on what comes back."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-guarantee-1qzlo4m"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Nobody can promise you funding, and anyone who does is telling you something about themselves. Here are the terms before you commit to anything."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"No refunds, because a refund does not get your proposal funded — it just ends the relationship with the deadline still on your desk. What we offer instead is the thing that actually helps: we keep working on it."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Unlimited revisions, within the agreed scope"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"No cap on rounds and no clock on them inside the scope agreed. Co-investigators join late, a topic is reworded, a sponsor changes what it wants funded. We revise."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A page limit misread, a mandatory annexe missed, a budget category applied wrongly — if something we were responsible for puts the application at risk, correcting it is free and we say so first."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Delivered before the deadline"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Working drafts land early enough to be argued about, and the final document with days rather than hours in hand. Funding deadlines do not move, and portals are least reliable on the last afternoon."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Your decisions stay yours"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We advise, argue a view and tell you plainly when we disagree with a choice you want to make. What goes in your name is settled by you, every time."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"05"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Mutual NDA on request"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Signed before you send anything, in both directions, at no cost. Your question, your data and the fact that you are working with us stay confidential either way — and we will sign yours rather than insisting on ours."}</p></div> </div> <div className={"rate rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"rate__score"}> <b>{"9.4"}</b><span>{"/10"}</span> </div> <div className={"rate__body"}> <p className={"rate__t"}><span className={"rate__stars"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"★★★★★"}</span>{" Average client rating"}</p> <p className={"rate__d"}>{"From "}<b>{"3,000 responses"}</b>{" to Pubrica’s own post-delivery survey, sent to every client at handover, January 2024 to June 2026. It is our figure, from our records, and we say so rather than borrowing a badge."}</p> </div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We cannot guarantee funding, and we will not quote a success rate as though it were one — outcomes depend on the panel, the budget and what else was submitted that round, none of which we control or can see. We will not write a proposal for a scheme you are not eligible for, and we check eligibility before quoting. We will not manufacture preliminary data, overstate what your pilot showed, or describe a collaboration that has not been agreed. And where we think an application is not worth the four months it will cost you, we will say so before you commission it rather than after."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"An expert reads the call free"}</p> <p>{"Before anything is quoted, a grant writing consultant reads your idea against the call and tells you whether you are eligible, whether the fit is genuine, and which criterion will be hardest for you. That conversation quite often ends with us pointing at a different scheme, and occasionally with us saying this one is not worth entering — which is unwelcome in week one and considerably better than in month five."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Scored against the funder’s own criteria"}</p> <p>{"Every review report uses the scale the funder publishes rather than a rating invented for the report, and where a funder publishes no scale — Wellcome and ICMR both publish criteria without one — we say so and assess against the criteria instead of supplying a number that would look authoritative and mean nothing."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"GDPR and data privacy"}</p> <p>{"Pubrica works with researchers in India, across the United Kingdom and Europe, in North America, throughout Asia-Pacific and the Middle East, and in Africa and Latin America, and every project is handled the same way wherever it comes from. An unfunded proposal is among the most sensitive documents a research group owns. Yours is held under GDPR, kept only as long as the project needs it, never used to train anything, and never shared outside your project team — and we decline work where we are already writing a competing application to the same call."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"The application is yours"}</p> <p>{"We draft, review and edit. The science, the claims and the commitments are yours, and the application is submitted in your name by your institution. Every funder requires that the applicant is accountable for the proposal, and professional writing support is ordinary and disclosed where a funder asks about it. Any use of AI in drafting is declared to you, and we follow whatever your funder says about it."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-client-stories-bjy52r"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three applications, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named researcher has confirmed it in writing."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“What changed the application was being told which criterion was going to sink it. We had spent a month on the section that was already fine.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"CLINICAL"}<br />{"RESEARCH"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Grant"}<br />{"Proposal"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Dr Aarti Menon"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Principal investigator · United States"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Scheme"}</b><span>{"To be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Our consortium proposal was strong on the science and thin on the impact pathway, which we had treated as a closing paragraph. They rewrote it as three separate things, which is what the form was asking for.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"EUROPEAN"}<br />{"CONSORTIUM"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Impact"}<br />{"Pathway"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Dr Elena Petrova"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Research coordinator · Germany"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Scheme"}</b><span>{"To be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“The word limits were the whole problem. Getting a rationale that needed a page into five hundred words was the work, and it was not work we knew how to do.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"BIOMEDICAL"}<br />{"RESEARCH"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"National"}<br />{"Funding"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Dr Nishant Reddy"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Research director · India"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Scheme"}</b><span>{"To be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-grant-writing-faq-1i78pro"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Grant writing FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Ten questions applicants ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure which call to aim at, or whether the draft you have will survive a panel? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-0"}><span>{"How can I structure a grant proposal to increase funding success?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Structure it around the funder’s criteria rather than around a generic outline, because the criteria are the order in which it will be read and scored. The sections almost every scheme wants are a title and summary, the background and the gap, a problem statement, objectives or specific aims, the methodology, a timeline, a budget with its justification, the expected outcomes and impact, and the supporting documents. What differs — and what decides the outcome — is the weight each one carries. A Horizon Europe proposal gives a third of its assessment to impact, so impact is a major section with its own structure. An ERC proposal has no impact criterion at all, and the same pages are better spent on the idea. An NIH Research Strategy has twelve pages for significance, innovation and approach, and nothing else scores. Write to the rubric, then check the structure against the funder’s template rather than against the last proposal you wrote."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-1"}><span>{"What are the key components of a compelling grant application?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"A problem a reviewer can verify is real, objectives that are specific and not contingent on one another, a methodology detailed enough that its feasibility can be judged, outcomes stated as things that will be true rather than things that will be attempted, a budget that visibly buys the workplan, a timeline with dependencies in it, and an explicit line connecting all of that to what this funder has said it wants. Two components carry more weight than applicants expect. The first is the alternative approach: naming what happens if the central method fails is what separates a proposal that reads as feasible from one that reads as hopeful. The second is the justification of the team — why these people, with this combination of methods, rather than any other group who could have proposed this."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-2"}><span>{"How do professional grant writing services help improve proposal quality?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Mostly by reading it as a reviewer will rather than as its author does. A professional grant writing service brings three things you cannot easily supply yourself: familiarity with the rubric that will be applied, including what this funder does not assess; a reader who has never seen the project and therefore notices where the argument is assumed rather than made; and the discipline of ranking changes by what each is worth instead of by how satisfying it is to make. Alongside that sits the unglamorous half of the work — eligibility, page limits, formatting, annexes, CV formats, budget categories and portal fields — which ends more applications than weak science does and which nobody enjoys doing at eleven at night. What it does not do is improve the research. If the idea is not competitive for this scheme, a better document makes that clearer rather than less clear, and we would rather say so early."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-3"}><span>{"What common mistakes should be avoided in grant proposals?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Eight, in roughly the order we see them. Writing to the wrong funder, so the document answers criteria nobody is applying. Objectives that depend on one another, so a reviewer who doubts the first doubts all of them. A methodology written at the level of a published paper’s methods section, which is far too thin to judge feasibility from. A sample size stated as a number, with the assumptions behind it missing. Impact treated as a closing paragraph where it is a scored criterion with a threshold. A budget fitted to the ceiling rather than built from the work. Reviewer comments from a previous round left visibly unanswered. And leaving the annexes until last — letters of support, data management plans and ethics self-assessments are where applications fail on the final afternoon. Six of those eight are decided before any drafting starts."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-4"}><span>{"How can expert guidance help align research goals with funding requirements?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"By starting from what the funder has said it will buy and working back to your project, which is the opposite of how most applications are written. That means reading the call text and the work programme rather than the scheme’s homepage, looking at what this funder has recently paid for in your area, and being honest about the distance between your question and its priorities. Sometimes the alignment is real and simply has not been stated, and saying it plainly in the first paragraph is most of the work. Sometimes the alignment is partial, and the project can be reframed or the scope adjusted without distorting the science. And sometimes there is no alignment, in which case the useful guidance is which other scheme fits — a redirection that costs an hour and saves four months. Expert guidance is worth most at that first decision and least once drafting is under way."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-5"}><span>{"How do I choose between funders, and does it really change the document?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"It changes it completely, which is why the same proposal sent to two funders usually loses at both. The published rubrics genuinely disagree. At the ERC, excellence is the sole criterion of evaluation and the first step reads only a five-page synopsis and a four-page CV — your methodology and your workplan are not in front of the panel yet. At Horizon Europe, impact is one of three equally weighted criteria, each with a threshold of 3 out of 5, so an outstanding proposal with a thin impact section is rejected on that alone. At NIH, the current framework scores the importance of the research and the rigour of the approach separately, and instructs reviewers that the importance score sets the limit on the best possible overall impact score. At ICMR, the whole rationale has to fit in five hundred words. Choose the funder first, from eligibility and genuine fit, then write one document properly for it."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-6"}><span>{"How long does a proposal take to write properly?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"For a major research grant, plan on three months from a standing start and treat six weeks as the minimum that does not compromise the document. The drafting itself is a smaller part of that than people expect. The long poles are the things that depend on other people: partner commitments and letters of support, institutional costings and approvals, ethics pre-checks, and getting co-investigators to send CVs in the funder’s format. A review of an existing draft takes about a week, which is why it is worth commissioning three or four weeks out rather than three days out. If you have less time than this, say so at the first conversation — we will tell you honestly what can be done well in the time available, and occasionally that the honest answer is to aim at the next round instead."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-7"}><span>{"Do you prepare the budget, and can you justify it to the funder’s rules?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, built from the workplan rather than fitted to the ceiling, and costed to the categories the scheme uses — the cost principles in the Uniform Guidance at 2 CFR Part 200 for United States federal awards, Horizon Europe’s actual and unit cost categories, full economic costing in the United Kingdom, and recurring and non-recurring heads for Indian national funders. The justification matters more than the arithmetic: a reviewer is asking whether the money buys the work, not whether the total is modest, and an under-costed proposal reads as naive rather than as good value. We work alongside your research office or finance team rather than around them, because the institutional rate agreements and approvals are theirs and the final figures have to be ones your institution will sign."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-8"}><span>{"What happens if the proposal is rejected?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"First, read the critique as evidence rather than as a verdict, and give it a week before deciding anything. Most summary statements contain three kinds of comment: criticisms that are factually answerable, criticisms that point at a real weakness, and criticisms that reveal a reviewer misread something — which is usually a writing problem rather than a reviewer problem, and is the most fixable of the three. Then the question is whether to resubmit, redirect or stop. Resubmission rules differ: NIH allows one resubmission with an introduction answering the previous critique, and a C grade at the ERC carries a restriction on reapplying that a B does not. A resubmission that does not visibly answer the earlier comments tends to attract them again, so the introduction is worth as much care as any section. Sometimes the right answer is that the proposal was fine and the call was wrong, and it should go elsewhere largely unchanged."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-9"}><span>{"Will Pubrica be named on the application, and is this ghostwriting?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-9"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and no. The application is submitted in your name by your institution, and the applicant is accountable for it — every funder requires that, and it is a condition rather than a formality. What we provide is drafting, review and editing support, which is ordinary in research and is used by a great many funded groups. Where a funder asks whether professional assistance was used, the answer is yes and we help you say so. What we will not do is invent preliminary data, describe a collaboration that has not been agreed, overstate what a pilot showed, or write claims you cannot stand behind at interview — and an interview is exactly where an overwritten proposal comes apart, because the panel asks about the sentence you did not write. Any use of AI in drafting is declared to you, and we follow whatever your funder’s policy says about it."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-10"}><span>{"Am I eligible?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-10"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Worth establishing before anything else, because it is checkable in an afternoon and it is the failure that ends four months of work. Three of the rules moved during 2026: both ERC career windows widened for the 2027 calls, so the familiar two-to-seven and seven-to-twelve year figures are now historic; NIH restructured how international collaborations are funded; and Wellcome’s geographic eligibility narrows on 29 October 2026. You can run the mechanical part yourself in the "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/free-tools/#grant-eligibility"} data-nav={""}>{"free grant eligibility checker"}</a>{", which prints the published rule beside its answer for eight schemes. We check it in the first conversation, before any writing is quoted."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-11"}><span>{"How far ahead should I start?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-11"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"For a single-investigator proposal, eight to twelve weeks before the deadline is comfortable and four is tight but survivable. For a consortium, four to six months, because the constraint is never the writing — it is assembling letters of support, agreeing the budget across partners, and getting institutional sign-off from organisations with their own internal deadlines. What actually goes wrong at the end is rarely the science: it is a partner who has not returned their section, a finance office that needs ten working days, and a portal that closes at a time zone nobody checked. Those are all solvable at week ten and not at day three."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-12"}><span>{"Do you write the data management plan and the impact section?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-12"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and they are worth more attention than they usually get. A data management plan is assessed against the funder’s own policy and against FAIR principles, and a generic one is visibly generic; it has to name the data types, the repositories, the metadata standard, the retention period and who is responsible. Impact under Horizon Europe is a third of the assessment and a hard gate, and it is scored on pathway and measures rather than on ambition. Both are rewritten per funder rather than carried across, because a section written for one framework frequently earns nothing at all under another."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-13"}><span>{"Do you write for industry, charity and national funders as well?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-13"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes. Applications have been written or reviewed for twenty-seven funders across the United States, Europe, the United Kingdom and India, including the major national agencies, the European frameworks, the large medical research charities, and the SBIR and STTR programmes. The differences between them are not cosmetic. A charity panel that includes patient reviewers reads a lay summary as a scored section rather than a formality. An SBIR proposal is assessed on commercial potential as well as science. A national agency in India may ask for the health-outcome case in five hundred words. We write to the rubric that will be used, which means the document is different each time."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"gw-14"}><span>{"How is a resubmission different from a first submission?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"gw-14"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"It is a different document with a different reader, and treating it as a revised first submission is why resubmissions fail twice. The panel has the previous summary statement, and the introduction to the resubmission is where the application is won or lost: it has to acknowledge each substantive criticism, say what changed, and — where you disagree — say so with evidence rather than absorbing the point silently. Reviewers notice both evasion and capitulation. It also matters that the science moved: a resubmission with new preliminary data addressing the central concern is a far stronger case than the same proposal written more carefully."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of a proposal."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A proposal needs a gap behind it and a design inside it, and both of those are work in their own right."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"BEFORE THE PROPOSAL"}</b><em>{"establishing there is a question"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Literature review and gap analysis"}</b><span>{"The gap stated so a reviewer can verify it, rather than asserted in an opening paragraph."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/systematic-review/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Systematic review"}</b><span>{"The registered synthesis that establishes what is known before you ask to add to it."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"INSIDE THE PROPOSAL"}</b><em>{"the methods a panel will score"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Experimental design"}</b><span>{"The study the proposal is promising to run, designed before it is described."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Biostatistics and statistical programming"}</b><span>{"The power calculation with its assumptions shown, which is what makes it checkable."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"AFTER THE AWARD"}</b><em>{"reporting what it found"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/peer-review-pre-submission/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Pre-submission peer review"}</b><span>{"The same mock-panel idea, applied to the manuscript the grant produces."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/journal-selection/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Journal selection"}</b><span>{"Where the work lands, decided from the manuscript rather than from habit."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on structure and journals."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library on how research is structured, placed and written."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the call and the idea. An expert will read it before we quote."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Whether you are eligible, whether the fit is real, and which criterion will be hardest for you specifically — in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation. If a different scheme suits the work better, that is what you will hear."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
